This statement is a check to ensure that the `Count` of elements in the ArrayList is always within the range of 0 to the capacity of the ArrayList, which in turn represents the size of the internal array used to hold items. This could prevent cases where the `Count` becomes larger than the `Capacity`, which is not valid. It also ensures that the `Count` does not become negative, which is also not logical. This may help to catch some error cases in our code.
