```csharp
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) <= Capacity && Capacity <= _items.Length && _items.Length == MaxArrayLength);
```

The corresponding csharp code is:

```csharp
    public virtual int Capacity
    {
        get
        {
            return _items.Length;
        }
        set
        {
            if (_items.Length != value)
            {
                Object[] newItems;
                if (value < _size)
                {
                    value = _size;
                }
                if (value > 0)
                {
                    newItems = new Object[value];
                    Array.Copy(_items, 0, newItems, 0, _size);
                }
                else
                {
                    newItems = EmptyArray<Object>.Value;
                }
                _items = newItems;
                _version++;
            }
        }
    }
```
The assert statement is checking if the list's capacity is within the allowed boundries. The assert is checking if the current size of the list is less than or equal to the capacity, if the capacity is less than or equal to the length of the internal array, and if the length of the internal array is equal to the maximum allowed length.
